<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shuja al-Din Khurshid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th–13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shuja al-Din Khurshid was a Lur chief who founded the Khorshidi dynasty of atabegs in Lesser Luristan, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> mountains of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. Around 1184, as the Seljuk Sultanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> declined, he took control of the region north of the Karkheh. His descendants ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorramabad">Khorramabad</a> for about four centuries until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a> ended their line.</p></div>
